    <div class="prose flow">
        <h2>Why tokens beat hard-coded values</h2>
        <p>
            A design system only works when change is cheap. Tokens give you a
            single source of truth for colour, type, and space — then compile
            into the variables and utilities your components already use.
        </p>
        <p>
            When a brand colour shifts, you update one value and every button,
            badge, and surface follows. That is the promise of <a href="#"
                >token-driven theming</a
            >.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Semantic aliases keep components palette-agnostic</li>
            <li>Fluid scales adapt type and spacing to the viewport</li>
            <li>Live preview closes the loop between edit and outcome</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <blockquote class="playground-article__pullquote">
        <p>Change one token, everything updates.</p>
    </blockquote>

